1
00:00:01,559 --> 00:00:03,080
[♪♪]

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,800
I'm Peppa Pig.

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,920
This is my little brother,
George.

4
00:00:06,920 --> 00:00:08,119
[SNORTS]

5
00:00:08,119 --> 00:00:10,479
This is Mommy Pig.
[SNORTS]

6
00:00:10,479 --> 00:00:11,879
And this is Daddy Pig.

7
00:00:11,879 --> 00:00:13,320
[SNORTS]
[ALL LAUGH]

8
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,680
Peppa Pig.

9
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:15,920
[GRUNTS]

10
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:20,160
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

11
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:23,360
NARRATOR:
Peppa and her friends
are at their playgroup.

12
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:26,799
Today we are going
to make a time capsule.

13
00:00:26,799 --> 00:00:29,360
[SNORTS]
What's a time capsule?

14
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:33,800
A time capsule is something that
will show people in the future

15
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,160
how we lived.
How?

16
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:38,680
We'll put special things
in this box,

17
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:42,480
and then we'll bury it
in the school garden.

18
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:44,400
Will it grow?
[ALL LAUGH]

19
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,879
MADAME GAZELLE:
No, Suzy.

20
00:00:45,879 --> 00:00:49,879
It will remain in the ground
for many years.

21
00:00:49,879 --> 00:00:51,680
ALL:
Ooh!

22
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:54,919
Now, what things
should we put inside?

23
00:00:54,919 --> 00:00:56,440
[SNORTS]
A comic.

24
00:00:56,440 --> 00:00:58,559
Very good, Peppa.

25
00:00:58,559 --> 00:01:00,640
[BLEATS]
Music.

26
00:01:00,640 --> 00:01:02,680
Very good, Suzy.

27
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:04,200
[BARKS]
A toy.

28
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:06,039
[NEIGHS]
A coin.

29
00:01:06,039 --> 00:01:07,840
[WHINNIES]
Stamps.

30
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:09,479
[SQUEAKS]
A carrot?

31
00:01:09,479 --> 00:01:11,080
[LAUGHS]

32
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:14,360
MADAME GAZELLE:
You do like carrots,
don't you, Rebecca?

33
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:15,600
Yes.

34
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:17,160
[ALL LAUGH]

35
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:21,399
All those are excellent things
to show our daily lives.

36
00:01:21,399 --> 00:01:25,280
Madame Gazelle,
what will the future be like?

37
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:28,039
MADAME GAZELLE:
What do you think
it will be like?

38
00:01:28,039 --> 00:01:31,560
I think in the future
I will live on the moon.

39
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:33,600
[GIGGLES]

40
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:36,880
And all my friends
will come to visit.

41
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:38,360
[ALL LAUGH]

42
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:41,320
[BARKS]

43
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:43,600
And I will fly
a space rocket.

44
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:45,600
Hello.
[ALL LAUGH]

45
00:01:52,839 --> 00:01:56,720
Now we'll record a message
for the people of the future.

46
00:01:56,720 --> 00:01:59,479
Say hello
to the future.

47
00:01:59,479 --> 00:02:01,479
Hello to the future.

48
00:02:01,479 --> 00:02:05,080
You're probably
all living on the moon now.

49
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:07,199
And going on holiday
to Mars.

50
00:02:07,199 --> 00:02:10,359
And flying around
in space rockets.

51
00:02:10,359 --> 00:02:12,880
[ALL LAUGH]

52
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:14,920
Wonderful.

53
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:18,440
It is nearly home time,

54
00:02:18,440 --> 00:02:20,640
and all the parents
have arrived. 

55
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:24,040
Mommy, Daddy, we've made
a time capsule.

56
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:25,600
Ah, Daddy Pig.

57
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:28,400
You're just in time
to help us dig a hole.

58
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:30,440
Yes, of course.

59
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:36,239
Daddy Pig is digging
a hole in the school garden,

60
00:02:36,239 --> 00:02:38,120
for the time capsule.

61
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,280
There.

62
00:02:43,280 --> 00:02:44,679
Can we dig it up now?

63
00:02:44,679 --> 00:02:46,040
[LAUGHS]

64
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:50,320
It will remain in the ground
for many years.

65
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:53,200
Oh, but I can't wait
that long.

66
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:56,840
Peppa, you are just like your
Daddy was when he was little.

67
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:58,160
Am I?

68
00:02:58,160 --> 00:03:01,840
Yes, I remember
when I was his teacher.

69
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:03,760
Did you teach
my Daddy?

70
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:07,679
Yes. I taught all of your
mommies and daddies, didn't I?

71
00:03:07,679 --> 00:03:09,160
ALL:
Yes, Madame Gazelle.

72
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:10,399
[ALL LAUGH]

73
00:03:10,399 --> 00:03:12,720
When your mommies
and daddies were little,

74
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:15,079
they made a time capsule too.

75
00:03:15,079 --> 00:03:18,280
Yes, we did. We buried it
next to a little tree.

76
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,920
Can we dig it up?

77
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:23,480
Yes. I think we buried it
over here.

78
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:26,720
Oh. I thought it was
a much smaller tree.

79
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:29,239
Oh, it was
a long time ago.

80
00:03:29,239 --> 00:03:31,480
The tree has grown a bit
since then.

81
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:32,920
[ALL LAUGH]

82
00:03:35,959 --> 00:03:38,200
[METALLIC THUMP]
I've found something.

83
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:40,600
It's our old
time capsule.

84
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:42,200
ALL:
Hooray!

85
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:44,799
I can't wait to open it.
[ALL LAUGH]

86
00:03:44,799 --> 00:03:47,440
Stand back, children.

87
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:49,799
ALL:
Yes, Madame Gazelle.

88
00:03:49,799 --> 00:03:52,440
And what do we have here?

89
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:54,720
Oh, an old comic.

90
00:03:54,720 --> 00:03:56,720
That was my
favorite comic.

91
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:58,359
A tin toy.

92
00:03:58,359 --> 00:03:59,839
My favorite toy.

93
00:03:59,839 --> 00:04:01,160
Music.

94
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:03,040
My favorite record.

95
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:05,760
And a very old carrot.

96
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:07,200
That's mine.

97
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:08,959
What a good choice,
Mommy.

98
00:04:08,959 --> 00:04:10,200
[ALL LAUGH]

99
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:12,359
And a videotape

100
00:04:12,359 --> 00:04:15,079
of your mommies and daddies
when they were little.

101
00:04:15,079 --> 00:04:17,479
ALL:
Ooh.

102
00:04:17,479 --> 00:04:19,599
[GIGGLES]

103
00:04:19,599 --> 00:04:22,440
Who's the little piggy
in the glasses?

104
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:24,280
MOMMY PIG:
Oh, that's Daddy Pig.

105
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:25,599
Oh. And that's me.

106
00:04:25,599 --> 00:04:27,440
Hello to the future.

107
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:28,840
[GIGGLES AND SNORTS]

108
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:31,200
What a squeaky voice
you have.

109
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:32,640
[CHUCKLES]

110
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:36,080
You're probably living
on the moon now.

111
00:04:36,080 --> 00:04:37,760
Silly little Daddy Pig.

112
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:39,320
[ALL LAUGH]

113
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:41,159
NARRATOR:
Making time capsules

114
00:04:41,159 --> 00:04:42,440
is such fun,

115
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:45,320
and finding them
is even better.

116
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:52,039
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

117
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:57,440
NARRATOR:
Peppa and George
are going to the seaside

118
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:59,360
with Granny and Grandpa Pig.

119
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:00,880
[HORN HONKS]

120
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:02,640
[BOTH GIGGLE]

121
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,479
Peppa and George
love the seaside.

122
00:05:06,479 --> 00:05:10,000
Oh. Where's the sand gone?

123
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:14,200
There isn't any sand
on this beach, Peppa.

124
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:15,960
No sand?

125
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:19,680
But we wanted
to make sand castles.

126
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:22,840
Peppa and George
love making sand castles.

127
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:24,520
[SOBS]

128
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:27,880
Now now, George,
don't be upset.

129
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:30,000
There are lots
of exciting things to do

130
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,520
on this rocky beach.

131
00:05:31,520 --> 00:05:32,919
Like what?

132
00:05:32,919 --> 00:05:34,880
GRANDPA PIG:
When the sea goes out,

133
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:38,599
it leaves little pools
of water in amongst the rocks.

134
00:05:38,599 --> 00:05:41,280
They're called
rock pools.

135
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:43,240
GRANDPA PIG:
And in every rock pool,

136
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:47,880
there's something special
that the sea has left behind.

137
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:51,680
Ooh. I can see something
glittering.

138
00:05:53,440 --> 00:05:55,159
It's a coin.

139
00:05:55,159 --> 00:05:56,479
Wow.

140
00:05:56,479 --> 00:05:59,280
Maybe it's a pirate's
treasure?

141
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:00,840
ALL: Ooh.
[SNORTS]

142
00:06:00,840 --> 00:06:04,080
Let's make a collection
of all the things we find.

143
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:07,000
Yes. We'll put them
in George's bucket.

144
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,280
[SNORTS]

145
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:09,520
[BOTH LAUGH]

146
00:06:09,520 --> 00:06:10,840
[SNORTS]

147
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:13,159
What surprise
is waiting in this pool?

148
00:06:13,159 --> 00:06:16,560
There's nothing special
in this one.

149
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:18,080
[LAUGHS AND SNORTS]

150
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:20,799
There's always
something, Peppa.

151
00:06:20,799 --> 00:06:22,280
Look closer.

152
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:25,080
Ooh, there is something.

153
00:06:25,080 --> 00:06:27,799
Yes, it's a crab.

154
00:06:27,799 --> 00:06:29,400
Aah!

155
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:31,960
The crab is pinching
Grandpa Pig's finger.

156
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:33,359
Oh!

157
00:06:33,359 --> 00:06:34,719
Ouch.

158
00:06:34,719 --> 00:06:37,880
[SNORTS]
Naughty Mr. Crab.

159
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,320
[LAUGHS]

160
00:06:39,320 --> 00:06:40,479
Look, George.

161
00:06:40,479 --> 00:06:45,120
Mr. Crab
is walking sideways.

162
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:46,440
[GIGGLES]

163
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:48,240
George is pretending to be a
crab.

164
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:51,280
Peppa wants
to be a crab too.

165
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:53,200
We're naughty crabs.

166
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:54,799
Pinch. Pinch. Pinch.

167
00:06:54,799 --> 00:06:57,080
[GIGGLES]

168
00:06:57,080 --> 00:06:58,760
Pinch. Pinch. Pinch.

169
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:03,240
Help! There are two naughty
crabs trying to pinch me!

170
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:04,880
Pinch. Pinch. Pinch.

171
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:07,200
We're naughty crabs.

172
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:08,919
Pinch. Pinch. Pinch.

173
00:07:08,919 --> 00:07:10,520
[ALL LAUGH]

174
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:12,799
Shoo, shoo, shoo,
you naughty crabs.

175
00:07:12,799 --> 00:07:15,000
Go back to your little
rock pools.

176
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,440
Yes.
[SNORTS]

177
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:18,200
Let's look in more
rock pools.

178
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,520
[SNORTING]

179
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:23,520
What can you see?

180
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:25,120
A seashell.

181
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:26,840
Can you hear the sea
in it?

182
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:28,239
What do you mean?

183
00:07:28,239 --> 00:07:30,280
If you put a shell
to your ear,

184
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:32,359
you can hear the sea.

185
00:07:32,359 --> 00:07:34,599
[SOUND OF CRASHING WAVES]

186
00:07:35,719 --> 00:07:37,359
Wow.

187
00:07:37,359 --> 00:07:39,359
I can hear the sea.

188
00:07:39,359 --> 00:07:41,479
[SOUND OF CRASHING WAVES
RESUMES]

189
00:07:41,479 --> 00:07:43,000
[GIGGLES]

190
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:45,120
I love my seashell.

191
00:07:45,120 --> 00:07:48,359
George, can you find
a seashell too?

192
00:07:48,359 --> 00:07:50,359
[SNORTS AND GIGGLES]

193
00:07:50,359 --> 00:07:51,919
Shell!
[SNORTS]

194
00:07:51,919 --> 00:07:53,880
That's not a shell.

195
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:56,280
Oh.

196
00:07:56,280 --> 00:07:58,280
GRANDPA PIG:
Peppa's right.

197
00:07:58,280 --> 00:07:59,640
That's not a shell.

198
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:02,760
George has found
a fossil.

199
00:08:02,760 --> 00:08:04,479
What's a fossil?

200
00:08:04,479 --> 00:08:06,440
GRANDPA PIG:
A fossil is the remains

201
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:11,400
of an animal that lived long
ago, when there were dinosaurs.

202
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:12,799
[SNORTING]

203
00:08:12,799 --> 00:08:14,719
Dinosaur. Grrr.

204
00:08:14,719 --> 00:08:17,359
[SQUEALS]
[BOTH LAUGH]

205
00:08:17,359 --> 00:08:20,280
Rock pools are such fun.

206
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:24,960
Yes, they're fun for us
but not for this little fish.

207
00:08:24,960 --> 00:08:26,880
A fish? Where?

208
00:08:26,880 --> 00:08:28,440
Ooh.

209
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:29,880
Poor little fish.

210
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:31,239
She's trapped.

211
00:08:31,239 --> 00:08:32,919
Oh.
Oh?

212
00:08:32,919 --> 00:08:38,840
The little fish says she wants
to go back to the sea.

213
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:42,720
Maybe you could use
your bucket to rescue her.

214
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:44,640
PEPPA:
Yes.

215
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:48,040
Peppa is rescuing
the little fish in her bucket.

216
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:49,959
Don't worry, Mrs. Fish.

217
00:08:49,959 --> 00:08:52,880
You'll soon be back
with your friends.

218
00:08:55,920 --> 00:08:58,000
[SNORTS]
Bye-bye, Mrs. Fish.

219
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,800
[SNORTS]
Bye-bye.

220
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:05,160
[LAUGHS]

221
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:07,319
ALL:
Oh!

222
00:09:07,319 --> 00:09:08,880
[ALL LAUGH]

223
00:09:08,880 --> 00:09:11,280
I love rock pools.

224
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:13,079
[ALL LAUGHING]

225
00:09:19,079 --> 00:09:22,360
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

226
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:24,120
NARRATOR:
Mr. Bull, the binman,

227
00:09:24,120 --> 00:09:26,120
is collecting
the rubbish.

228
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:28,280
It is early morning,

229
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:31,560
so Mr. Bull tries to be
as quiet as he can.

230
00:09:32,520 --> 00:09:34,920
[CANS CLATTERING LOUDLY]

231
00:09:34,920 --> 00:09:38,160
But Mr. Bull is not very good
at being quiet.

232
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:42,600
Peppa and George
are finishing their breakfast.

233
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:44,800
[SNORTS]
What's that noise?

234
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:47,160
It's Mr. Bull, the binman.

235
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:50,319
[SNORTS]
Hello, Mr. Bull.

236
00:09:50,319 --> 00:09:51,839
Moo!

237
00:09:51,839 --> 00:09:53,280
Hello, everyone.

238
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:56,319
Must be off.
Lots of rubbish to collect.

239
00:09:56,319 --> 00:09:59,600
ALL: Bye!
[COUGHS] Bye.

240
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:01,920
Moo!

241
00:10:01,920 --> 00:10:05,880
Mr. Bull has emptied
the rubbish bin for us.

242
00:10:05,880 --> 00:10:08,640
Good. Let's clear up
the breakfast things.

243
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:10,360
Can we help, Mommy?

244
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:11,720
Yes, you can.

245
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:14,839
Let's throw this empty bottle
in the bin.

246
00:10:14,839 --> 00:10:16,880
Peppa, stop.
What?

247
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:19,240
We don't put bottles
in the rubbish bin.

248
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:21,800
They can be recycled.

249
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:23,400
What does that mean?

250
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:25,400
All the things
we can't use again

251
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:29,040
we put in the rubbish bin
for Mr. Bull.

252
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:31,560
But all the things
that can be used again

253
00:10:31,560 --> 00:10:34,199
are put in these
recycle boxes.

254
00:10:34,199 --> 00:10:36,640
DADDY PIG:
The red one is for newspapers,

255
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:38,880
the blue one is for tin cans

256
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:42,120
and the green one
is for bottles.

257
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:44,520
Peppa, you have a bottle.

258
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:46,920
So which box
does it go in?

259
00:10:46,920 --> 00:10:49,079
Um, the green one.

260
00:10:49,079 --> 00:10:51,000
MOMMY PIG:
Yes.

261
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,959
[GIGGLING]
This is fun.

262
00:10:52,959 --> 00:10:54,640
Now it's George's turn.

263
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:57,520
Can you find a newspaper
for the red box?

264
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:59,800
[SNORTS AND GIGGLES]

265
00:11:01,319 --> 00:11:04,000
George wants to recycle
Daddy Pig's newspaper.

266
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:06,400
[LAUGHING]
I haven't finished

267
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:08,800
with my newspaper
just yet, George.

268
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,680
You can have it
in a minute.

269
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:14,439
[SNORTS]
Oh, all right.

270
00:11:14,439 --> 00:11:15,959
Here you are, George.

271
00:11:15,959 --> 00:11:17,959
[SNORTS AND LAUGHS]

272
00:11:17,959 --> 00:11:20,680
Newspapers go
in the red box, George.

273
00:11:20,680 --> 00:11:22,000
[SNORTS]

274
00:11:23,079 --> 00:11:24,319
[BOTH LAUGH]

275
00:11:24,319 --> 00:11:26,560
Now that we have
collected enough things,

276
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:29,040
we can go
to the recycle center.

277
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:31,319
Hooray. Let's go.

278
00:11:32,839 --> 00:11:35,319
Mommy Pig has the bottles...
[CLANKING]

279
00:11:35,319 --> 00:11:37,680
...Peppa has the tin cans...
[RATTLING]

280
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:39,719
...and George has
the newspapers.

281
00:11:39,719 --> 00:11:42,439
[RUFFLING]

282
00:11:42,439 --> 00:11:44,000
Is everybody ready?

283
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,719
ALL:
Yes, Daddy Pig.

284
00:11:45,719 --> 00:11:48,000
Then let's go.

285
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,439
[CAR HORN HONKS]

286
00:11:50,360 --> 00:11:51,839
[RUBBISH RATTLING]

287
00:11:51,839 --> 00:11:55,360
♪ Recycle, recycle
We're going to recycle ♪

288
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:57,400
♪ Tin cans ♪
[RATTLING]

289
00:11:57,400 --> 00:11:59,880
♪ Bottles ♪
[CLANKING]

290
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:02,360
Newspapers.
[RUSTLING]

291
00:12:02,360 --> 00:12:04,199
[RUBBISH RATTLING]
[LAUGHS]

292
00:12:04,199 --> 00:12:06,719
♪ Recycle, recycle
We're going to recycle ♪

293
00:12:06,719 --> 00:12:08,600
[ALL LAUGH]

294
00:12:10,439 --> 00:12:13,760
This is Miss Rabbit's
recycle center.

295
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:16,160
We're here.
ALL: Hooray.

296
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:17,719
Hello, there.

297
00:12:17,719 --> 00:12:19,640
Hello, Miss Rabbit.

298
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:22,199
Have you come to do
some recycling?

299
00:12:22,199 --> 00:12:23,640
Yes, we have.

300
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:25,040
Jolly good.

301
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:26,680
[LIFT BEEPING]
Carry on.

302
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:29,319
PEPPA:
What's Miss Rabbit doing?

303
00:12:29,319 --> 00:12:31,199
DADDY PIG:
She's recycling

304
00:12:31,199 --> 00:12:33,400
all the rusty,
old cars.

305
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:36,079
PEPPA:
Wow!

306
00:12:37,959 --> 00:12:40,319
Who can tell me which bin
the bottles go in?

307
00:12:40,319 --> 00:12:42,439
The green one.

308
00:12:42,439 --> 00:12:43,719
That's right.

309
00:12:43,719 --> 00:12:45,240
[GLASS CLANKING]

310
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:47,959
And the cans
go in the blue one.

311
00:12:47,959 --> 00:12:49,319
Well done, Peppa.

312
00:12:49,319 --> 00:12:50,680
[RATTLING]

313
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:52,000
[SNORTS]

314
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,199
George wants to recycle
the newspapers.

315
00:12:54,199 --> 00:12:57,439
Okay, George, you can do
the newspapers.

316
00:12:57,439 --> 00:12:58,719
[GIGGLES]

317
00:12:58,719 --> 00:13:01,240
[ALL LAUGH]

318
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:02,760
There.

319
00:13:02,760 --> 00:13:05,079
That's enough
recycling for one day.

320
00:13:05,079 --> 00:13:07,640
Yes, let's go home.

321
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:09,040
[LAUGHING]

322
00:13:09,040 --> 00:13:11,480
Oh, where's our car gone?

323
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:13,480
Peppa's car
has disappeared.

324
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:15,280
Stand back!

325
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:17,920
Miss Rabbit is recycling
Peppa's car.

326
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:19,160
[ALL GASP]

327
00:13:19,160 --> 00:13:20,360
Stop!

328
00:13:20,360 --> 00:13:21,800
That's our car!

329
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:23,760
What? Is it really?

330
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:25,040
ALL:
Yes!

331
00:13:25,040 --> 00:13:28,079
Our car isn't
old and rusty.

332
00:13:28,079 --> 00:13:29,959
[LAUGHS]

333
00:13:29,959 --> 00:13:33,760
Silly me.
I just love recycling.

334
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:35,439
Yes. So do we.

335
00:13:35,439 --> 00:13:38,599
But we also love
little our car.

336
00:13:38,599 --> 00:13:41,520
Yes, and our little car
loves us too.

337
00:13:41,520 --> 00:13:43,280
Don't you?
[HORN HONKS]

338
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:45,599
[ALL LAUGH]

339
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:51,959
[PEPPA READING ONSCREEN TEXT]

340
00:13:51,959 --> 00:13:53,959
[DUCKS QUACKING]

341
00:13:53,959 --> 00:13:56,719
NARRATOR:
The ducks are swimming
in their pond.

342
00:13:56,719 --> 00:13:58,599
They are very happy.

343
00:14:00,079 --> 00:14:03,560
Here are Peppa, George,
Mommy Pig and Daddy Pig.

344
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:05,959
Hello, ducks.

345
00:14:05,959 --> 00:14:07,160
[QUACKING]

346
00:14:07,160 --> 00:14:08,640
The ducks want some bread.

347
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:12,280
Sorry, Mrs. Duck,
we haven't got any bread today.

348
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:15,479
We've got something
much more fun.

349
00:14:15,479 --> 00:14:18,079
Peppa has brought
her toy boat.

350
00:14:18,079 --> 00:14:19,800
[QUACKING]
[SNORTS]

351
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:22,439
And George has brought
his toy boat.

352
00:14:23,920 --> 00:14:26,800
Let's wind your boat up,
George.

353
00:14:28,599 --> 00:14:32,280
George's boat
works with clockwork.

354
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:34,360
Quick, George,
put the boat in the pond

355
00:14:34,360 --> 00:14:36,439
before the clockwork
runs out.

356
00:14:41,079 --> 00:14:42,439
[GIGGLES]

357
00:14:42,439 --> 00:14:43,719
[SNORTING]

358
00:14:43,719 --> 00:14:45,599
George loves his
clockwork boat.

359
00:14:45,599 --> 00:14:48,319
Mommy, can you wind
my boat up?

360
00:14:48,319 --> 00:14:50,760
Your boat doesn't need
winding up, Peppa.

361
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:54,560
Peppa's boat is a sailboat.
The wind makes it go along.

362
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:56,240
I don't like my boat.

363
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:57,439
[SNORTS]

364
00:14:57,439 --> 00:14:58,959
It doesn't do anything.

365
00:14:58,959 --> 00:15:01,360
That's because there isn't
any wind today.

366
00:15:01,360 --> 00:15:03,319
Maybe it just needs
a little help.

367
00:15:03,319 --> 00:15:05,400
I'll huff and I'll puff

368
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:07,439
and I'll blow
your boat along.

369
00:15:07,439 --> 00:15:10,920
[INHALING AND BLOWING]

370
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:14,360
[LAUGHING]
Hooray!

371
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:16,319
It went really fast.

372
00:15:16,319 --> 00:15:18,439
Peppa loves her sailboat.

373
00:15:18,439 --> 00:15:19,800
[BLEATING]

374
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:21,920
Here is Peppa's friend,
Suzy Sheep.

375
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:23,240
Hello, everyone.

376
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:24,599
Hello, Suzy.

377
00:15:24,599 --> 00:15:27,160
We're playing
with our boats.

378
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:28,319
[BLEATS]

379
00:15:28,319 --> 00:15:30,400
I've got my speedboat.

380
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:31,959
Is it clockwork?

381
00:15:31,959 --> 00:15:35,199
No. It has batteries.

382
00:15:35,199 --> 00:15:38,640
Suzy's speedboat uses batteries
to make it go.

383
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:40,319
Ooh.
Ooh.

384
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:44,079
What a great speedboat.

385
00:15:44,079 --> 00:15:46,040
[QUACKS]

386
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:47,959
Sorry, Mrs. Duck.

387
00:15:47,959 --> 00:15:49,160
[QUACKING]

388
00:15:49,160 --> 00:15:50,560
[BARKING]

389
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:52,520
Here is Danny Dog
with Granddad Dog.

390
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:55,079
Hello, everyone.
Hello, Danny.

391
00:15:55,079 --> 00:15:58,199
My Granddad has made me
this paddleboat.

392
00:15:58,199 --> 00:15:59,959
ALL:
Ooh.

393
00:16:01,719 --> 00:16:03,719
I say.
That's impressive.

394
00:16:03,719 --> 00:16:05,319
[SNORTS]
How does it work?

395
00:16:05,319 --> 00:16:07,599
It's steam-powered.

396
00:16:07,599 --> 00:16:10,079
I just push
this little lever.

397
00:16:10,079 --> 00:16:11,439
[TOOTS]

398
00:16:11,439 --> 00:16:13,120
ALL:
Wow.

399
00:16:13,120 --> 00:16:15,520
What a fantastic
paddleboat.

400
00:16:15,520 --> 00:16:17,000
[QUACKING]

401
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:19,920
[SQUEAKING]

402
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:22,040
Here is Rebecca Rabbit
with her mommy.

403
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:23,240
Hello, everyone.

404
00:16:23,240 --> 00:16:24,640
Hello, Rebecca.

405
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:27,160
We're playing
with our boats.

406
00:16:33,479 --> 00:16:35,359
I wish I had a boat.

407
00:16:35,359 --> 00:16:37,640
Rebecca Rabbit
does not have a boat.

408
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:39,000
I've got an idea.

409
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,479
Luckily I brought
my newspaper along.

410
00:16:41,479 --> 00:16:44,400
I just need one page.

411
00:16:44,400 --> 00:16:45,920
Which page can we lose?

412
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:48,160
News? Sport?

413
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:49,800
Ah, fashion.

414
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,439
Not the fashion page.

415
00:16:51,439 --> 00:16:53,680
Okay, I'll use
the business page.

416
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,680
When I was
a little piggy,

417
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:59,560
I used to fold newspaper
like this.

418
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:02,520
What is Daddy Pig doing?

419
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:04,079
To make a paper boat.

420
00:17:04,079 --> 00:17:06,280
Daddy Pig has made
a paper boat.

421
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,480
[SQUEAKS]

422
00:17:07,480 --> 00:17:08,680
Thank you, Mr. Pig.

423
00:17:08,680 --> 00:17:10,319
[CHUCKLES]
[SNORTS]

424
00:17:10,319 --> 00:17:12,560
George wants
a paper boat too.

425
00:17:12,560 --> 00:17:13,839
[DADDY PIG LAUGHS]

426
00:17:13,839 --> 00:17:17,599
I suppose I can do
without the sports page.

427
00:17:17,599 --> 00:17:19,720
[SNORTS AND LAUGHS]

428
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:21,000
Please can I have one?

429
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:22,359
And me.
And me.

430
00:17:22,359 --> 00:17:24,119
[LAUGHS]
Of course.

431
00:17:24,119 --> 00:17:27,599
Daddy Pig is making
paper boats for everyone.

432
00:17:27,599 --> 00:17:29,399
Let's have a race.

433
00:17:29,399 --> 00:17:30,960
Good idea, Mommy Pig.

434
00:17:30,960 --> 00:17:34,600
We can huff and puff
and blow the paper boats across.

435
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:36,680
Everyone take
a deep breath.

436
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:38,159
[ALL INHALE]

437
00:17:38,159 --> 00:17:40,200
Ready? Steady?

438
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:42,000
Blow!

439
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,040
[ALL BLOWING]

440
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:47,680
We have a winner.

441
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:50,159
Uh, who had
the sports page?

442
00:17:50,159 --> 00:17:52,240
That's George's boat.

443
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:53,440
George is the winner.

444
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:54,720
ALL:
Hooray!

445
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:56,360
[ALL GIGGLE]

446
00:17:56,360 --> 00:17:58,159
I like boats.

447
00:17:58,159 --> 00:18:01,040
And I like
paper boats the best.

448
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:02,320
ALL:
Me too!

449
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:03,720
[ALL LAUGH]

450
00:18:03,720 --> 00:18:05,440
It's time to go home.

451
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:07,200
Everybody has had
a great time.

452
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:08,800
ALL:
Bye-bye!

453
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:10,280
Bye-bye, ducks.

454
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:11,800
See you soon.

455
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:13,639
The ducks enjoyed
the toy boats.

456
00:18:13,639 --> 00:18:15,639
But they quite like
having the pond

457
00:18:15,639 --> 00:18:17,040
back to themselves again.

458
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:18,919
[QUACKING]

459
00:18:20,080 --> 00:18:21,720
[PEPPA LAUGHING AND SNORTING]

460
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:23,080
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

461
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:25,600
[SNORTING AND LAUGHING]

462
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:27,639
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

463
00:18:27,639 --> 00:18:29,840
[SNORTING AND LAUGHING]

464
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:32,000
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

465
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,800
[SNORTING AND LAUGHING]

